.TH QUADLET-COMPOSE 1 "August 2026" "quadlet-compose 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quadlet-compose \- generate and manage systemd units from Podman Compose files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadlet-compose
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.PP
.B complet
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadlet-compose
(also available as
.BR complet )
converts Docker Compose files into systemd units managed by Podman.
It handles generation, installation, enable/disable, and lifecycle operations
for rootless or system-wide containers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Show help for any command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information.
.TP
.B \-\-user
Operate in user mode (systemctl --user). This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-system
Operate in system mode (systemctl --system).
.SH COMMANDS
.SS gen <compose-file>
Generate a systemd unit from a compose file and print to stdout (dry-run mode).
.PP
Flags:
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-name \fINAME\fR
Override service name (default: compose project name).
.TP
.B \-\-after \fIUNIT\fR
Additional After= dependencies (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-env-file \fIPATH\fR
EnvironmentFile= paths (repeatable).
.TP
.B \-\-timeout \fISECONDS\fR
TimeoutStartSec value (default: 120).
.TP
.B \-\-compose-bin \fICOMMAND\fR
Compose binary command (default: /usr/bin/podman compose).
.RE
.SS install <compose-file>
Generate and install a systemd unit, then daemon-reload.
Accepts the same flags as
.BR gen .
.SS enable <compose-file>
Install, enable, and start the systemd unit. Accepts the same flags as
.BR gen .
.SS disable <name>
Disable and stop a managed unit.
.SS remove <name>
Disable, delete the unit file, and daemon-reload.
.SS list
List all managed units with their source and status.
.SS status <name>
Show systemctl status for a managed unit.
.SS logs <name> [\-\- extra-flags]
Show journalctl logs for a managed unit. Extra flags after
.B \-\-
are passed to journalctl.
.SS completions <shell>
Generate shell completion scripts. Supported shells: bash, zsh, fish.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/containers/systemd/
User-mode unit directory where generated units are installed.
.TP
.I /etc/containers/systemd/
System-mode unit directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/containers/compose/
Default compose file directory for
.BR complet-generator (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Preview a unit without installing:
.RS
.nf
quadlet-compose gen docker-compose.yml
.fi
.RE
.PP
Install and enable a stack:
.RS
.nf
complet enable ./my-app/docker-compose.yml
.fi
.RE
.PP
List managed units:
.RS
.nf
complet list
.fi
.RE
.PP
View logs:
.RS
.nf
complet logs my-app -- -f --since "5 min ago"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove a managed unit:
.RS
.nf
complet remove my-app
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR complet-generator (1),
.BR podman-compose (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
